---
title: Lamb Kefedes
servings: 6
course: Main
prep time: 20m
cook time: 10m
locale: en
difficulty: Medium
cuisine: Greek
---

= Meatballs =

Put all the ingredients (@lamb mince{675%g}, @fesh breadcrumbs{75%g}, @egg{1}, @onion{1%large}(grated), @garlic{2%cloves}(crushed), @salt, @black pepper{}(ground), and @mixed fresh herbs (mint, parsley){8%tbsp}(chopped)) into a large bowl and mix together. Using your hands, divide the mixture into six portions. Take each portion and squeeze it along a flat metal skewer to make a sausage shape, 15-20 centimetres long. Cover and chill for ~{2%hours}, or longer if wished.

Brush the meat with a little @olive oil{}, then cook over a medium-high heat for 8 to ~{10%minutes}, turning occasionally, until cooked through.

= Serve =

Serve with @pita bread{}, @shredded lettuce{}, @cucumber{}(sliced), and @natural yoghurt{} with @mint{}(chopped) mixed into it.